                        only the even numbers in a list.

                    </li>

                    <li class="mb-2">

                        <strong>Squares:</strong>

                        <br>

                        <code>map()</code> using <code>map()</code> and lambda to find the square of
                        each number in a list.

                    </li>

                    <li class="mb-2">

                        <strong>Student Marks:</strong>

                        <br>

                        Use lambda and <code>filter()</code> to find
                        40 students with marks greater than or equal to 40.

                    </li>

                    <li>

                        <strong>Course Fee Sorting:</strong>

                        <br>

                        Use lambda and <code>sort()</code> to find
                        sort CIIT courses in ascending order based on their fees.

                    </li>

                </ol>

            </div>


            <!-- =========================
                 SUMMARY
            ========================== -->

            <div class="alert alert-info mt-4 mb-0"
                 style="background-color:#cfe2ff; border:0; color:#123c73;">

                <h2 class="h3 fw-bold mt-0 mb-3"
                    style="color:#123c73;">

                    Summary :

                </h2>

                <p class="mb-0"
                   style="color:#123c73;">

                    A lambda function in Python is a short anonymous function that
                    generally performs a single expression.
                    The syntax of a lambda is <strong>lambda arguments: expression</strong> hota hai.
                    It is commonly used for short calculations and conditions, along with
                    <strong>map(), filter() aur sorted()</strong> functions
                    ke saath commonly kiya jata hai.

                </p>

            </div>


